                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>SSHIFT</name>
                <description>Sample shift
By default, the HSPI samples data 1/2 of a CLK cycle after the data is driven by the external device.
This bit allows the data to be sampled later in order to consider the external signal delays.
The software must ensure that SSHIFTÂ =Â 0 when the data phase is configured in DTR mode (when DDTRÂ =Â 1.)</description>
