              <description>BSMX Active flag Set and cleared by hardware. This flag must be used by the application in order to check if the BSMX is effectively enabled (active) or not. BSSEL[4:0] can only be updated when the BSMXACTIVE is set to    a   . The BSMXACTIVE flag is a logical     between OLDACTIVE, DFLTACTIVE, and SCDACTIVE flags. Both of them must be set to     in order update BSSEL[4:0] field. - 0: The BSMX is not active, and can be configured if needed - 1: The BSMX is active, and protected fields cannot be configured.</description>
              <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
